roid problems, or other metabolic issues.\n  2. **Cardiovascular / blood pressure-related factors**, especially since your stored record shows persistent hypertension treatment and prior elevated readings.\n  3. **Medication or recovery burden**, depending on when symptoms worsened relative to treatment changes.\n  4. **Sleep-related causes** such as poor sleep quality or sleep apnea, which can cause progressive daytime exhaustion over months.\n- Your DNA/EHR profile gives useful background risk, but your current symptom still needs targeted follow-up questions before any stronger interpretation.\n- This is a **preliminary indicator**, not a final diagnosis.\n\n### Recommended questions\nAnswering these will help narrow it down.\n\n**(1/4)** Have you also noticed any of these along with the exhaustion: **shortness of breath, dizziness, palpitations, headaches, swelling in the legs, poor sleep/snoring, weight change, or reduced exercise tolerance**?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0eaa06dc42aeace00169ca644da09081918499e3784f8f7057\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":6756,"output":493,"cacheRead":14208,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21457,"cost":{"input":0.016890000000000002,"output":0.0073950000000000005,"cacheRead":0.003552,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.027837}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774871623671}}
