changes: more stress and less sleep.\\n- User reports blood pressure has seemed a bit low at times, but exact readings unknown.\\n- Denies chest pain, shortness of breath, fainting, and new vision changes.\\n\\nStored EHR/KLM context:\\n- 48-year-old male.\\n- Diagnoses: hypertension / uncontrolled hypertension; chronic kidney disease stage 2.\\n- Prior readings: BP 158/98 on 2025-10-10, HR 88 bpm, eGFR 71, UACR 135.\\n- Medications: lisinopril 20 mg, amlodipine 5 mg.\\n- Background genomic risk markers exist for hypertension and CKD progression.\\n\\nSimulated smartwatch telemetry summary:\\n- heart_rate_series only; no true beat-to-beat HRV metrics available.\\n- 17,280 samples.\\n- HR range 47.18 to 181.54 bpm.\\n- Mean HR 68.96 bpm; median 68.27 bpm; SD 17.63 bpm.\\n- Use caution: this is simulated wearable telemetry, not verified medical data.\\n\\nPlease return a patient-facing response with these sections:\\n1) Doctor Agent assessment\\n2) Most likely explanations\\n3) What should be checked next\\n4) When to seek urgent care\\n5) Brief reassurance/caution note\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":279,"output":474,"cacheRead":95360,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":96113,"cost":{"input":0.0006975000000000001,"output":0.00711,"cacheRead":0.02384,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0316475}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774872235614}}
